<text x="1493.52" y="505.46" size="2.54" layer="97" rot="MR180">Note: The AM62x ROM code requires CD 
to have an active-low polarity.  Depending 
on the CD polarity of the SD card holder
you may need to add an inverter as shown. </text>
<text x="12.7" y="688.34" size="2.54" layer="97" rot="MR180">GPMC[0:15] are used as boot mode pins and have default pull up / pull 
down behavior.  See "Boot Mode" section for more information.</text>
<text x="111.76" y="817.88" size="1.778" layer="150" rot="MR180" align="top-left">CS0</text>
<text x="111.76" y="815.34" size="1.778" layer="150" rot="MR180" align="top-left">CLK</text>
<text x="111.76" y="812.8" size="1.778" layer="150" rot="MR180" align="top-left">D0</text>
<text x="111.76" y="810.26" size="1.778" layer="150" rot="MR180" align="top-left">D1</text>
<text x="12.7" y="675.64" size="2.54" layer="97" rot="MR180">To meet the Mikroe Click standard, a resistor mux is used to add GPIO
functionality to the CLICK0_AN and CLICK1_AN pins.  This is generally 
not needed in a design based on the OSD62-PM-BRK.</text>
<text x="406.4" y="850.9" size="6.4516" layer="97">OLDI / LVDS Display Interface</text>
<text x="406.4" y="845.82" size="2.54" layer="97" rot="MR180">Based on AM62x SKEVM with Fulton PMIC</text>
<text x="406.4" y="840.74" size="2.54" layer="97" rot="MR180">Supports:  SK-LCD1 Interface (https://www.ti.com/tool/SK-LCD1)</text>
<text x="401.32" y="505.46" size="2.54" layer="97" rot="MR180">USBx_VBUS is a power sense 
input to the AM6254 and 
must be scaled (see AM6254
datasheet Section 9.2.3)</text>
<text x="406.4" y="820.42" size="2.54" layer="97" align="top-left">LVDS length requirements:
  - Inter pair:  0.15mm
  - Intra pair:  5mm</text>
<text x="1059.18" y="553.72" size="3.81" layer="150" align="top-left">I2C0 Pull-up Resistors</text>
<text x="1193.8" y="355.6" size="2.54" layer="97" rot="MR180">USBx_VBUS is a power sense 
input to the AM6254 and 
must be scaled (see AM6254
datasheet Section 9.2.3)</text>
